  "h1": [
    "Dr. Igal Elyassi"
  ],
  "word_count": 298,
  "body_markdown": "Follow\n\n(323) 433-5990\n\nHome\n\nServices\n\nAll-On-Four\n\nDental Implants\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nAbout\n\nFAQ\n\nForms\n\nBlog\n\nContact\n\n\n# Dr. Igal Elyassi\n\n\n\n## FOUNDER\n\n\nDr. Igal Elyassi graduated from University of Southern California School of Dentistry. Established Wilshire Smile Studio in 2002. He is the former president of the Los Angeles chapter of Alpha Omega International as well as an active member of the American Dental Association and California Dental Association.\n\nDr. Elyassi believes that dentistry is a partnership between patient and doctor; providing education on oral health to prevent dental problems, as well as clear explanations of treatment options. To offer the best possible patient care, he employs only the very best general and specialty dentists, assistants, hygienists, technicians, and office staff.\n\nHe also knows the importance of continuing education for himself and his staff at Wilshire Smile Studio. As a result, it is one of the most highly-rated smile makeover practices in Southern California; drawing patients from all over the world.\n\nDr. Elyassi loves to travel. He is a fan of the FC Barcelona soccer team and Los Angeles Laker. He favors sushi and Italian food, and says his favorite movie is “The Godfather”.\n\n\n## Contact Us\n\n\nFull Name *\n\nPhone\n\nMessage\n\nSubmit\n\nWE PROVIDE THIRD PARTY FINANCING\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-on-Four-Implants\n\n\n#### Useful Links\n\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\n6200 Wilshire Blvd., #1609\n\nLos Angeles, CA 90048\n\nCopyright © 2026. Wilshire Smile Studio. All Rights Reserved. The Dental Implant Center of Los Angeles offers sedation dentistry and dental implant surgery, also serving West Hollywood, Santa Monica, Beverly Hills, and more. | Sitemap | Privacy Policy\n\nSkip to content\n\nOpen toolbar\n\nAccessibility Tools\n\nIncrease Text\n\nDecrease Text\n\nGrayscale\n\nHigh Contrast\n\nNegative Contrast\n\nLight Background\n\nLinks Underline\n\nReadable Font\n\nReset",
